{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790262674,"nonce":"WgS8NFK3oZkXCHPIM45mpLIxuLI=","title":"Lua: a builtin the program assigns reads nil before the assignment","message":"A global named like a builtin that the program also assigns is no longer the builtin (builtin_named checks global_writes), and its module variable starts nil, so a read before the assignment finds nil where lua5.4 finds the library function.\n\n    local s = print\n    print = function(...) return s(...) end\n    print(\"hi\")\n\nlua5.4 prints hi; zylua (main dea6d08b and later) raises \"attempt to call a nil value (upvalue 's')\". The common wrapper idiom `local old = setmetatable; setmetatable = function(t, m) ... old(t, m) end` fails the same way. The module variable of an assigned builtin should start as the library function.","files":null}]}